# Nanalu Boutique — environment variables (template)
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#     cp .env.example .env.local
# `.env.local` is gitignored — real secrets NEVER get committed. This template
# is the committed contract: every variable the app reads should be listed here
# (with a safe placeholder), so a fresh clone knows what to set.
#
# Nothing below is required YET — the app runs with no env vars today. These are
# placeholders for services we'll wire up in later phases (see PLAN.md). Each
# stays commented out until the code that reads it actually lands.

# — Database: PostgreSQL via Prisma (Phase 1+) —
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/nanalu?schema=public"

# — Image storage: Cloudinary (swappable later via an image-access layer) —
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=""
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=""
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=""

# — Payments: Stripe (card data goes browser → Stripe; we store only tokens) —
# Publishable key is exposed to the browser, hence the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# The secret key is server-only — never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# — Auth (vetted provider, TBD — never hand-rolled) —
# AUTH_SECRET=""
